<title>GREECE: Greek PM announces tax on T-bills, tough budget.</title>
<headline>Greek PM announces tax on T-bills, tough budget.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Costas Simitis said Greece will start taxing interest earned on Treasury bills and bonds, sharply cut spending and hiring and abolish many existing tax exemptions.</p>
<p>Simitis made his statements after a cabinet meeting on the 1997 budget, which must be submitted to parliament by the end of this month.</p>
